# Platform Date on the live CLI

Same assemblage as `examples/platform_date.wcn`, but Target is `%cli-live`.
`Date` is born as a real JavaScript `Date` via the live interpreter’s host
constructor registry (`new Date(y, m, d, h, min, sec)` — month is 0-based),
because Target declares `Date::CONSTRUCT`.

## Schema

```
Person = String/name Date/dob
```

## Construction

```
[:Person "Ada" [:Date 1815 11 10 0 0 0]]
```

## Methods

```
Person::bornYear = { dob.getFullYear() }

Person::caption = {
  y = this.bornYear().
  name.concat(" born ").concat(y.str())
}

Person::withDob = { Int/y, Int/m, Int/d |
  [:Person name [:Date y m d 0 0 0]]
}
```

## Target

```
%cli-live

%requires
Date
Date::CONSTRUCT(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) -> Date
Date::getFullYear() -> Int

%init
var person;

function init() {
    person = PersonAssemblage.factory();
    wchntConsole.println(person.caption());
    wchntConsole.println(person);
    wchntConsole.println("enter to rebuild withDob(1970, 0, 1)");
}

%step
function step(line) {
    person = person.withDob(1970, 0, 1);
    wchntConsole.println(person.caption());
    wchntConsole.println(person);
}
```
